Session 337 summary — the D-513 rig phase produced one major pass and uncovered a new critical defect:

**Natural incident-513 refusal contained (PASS).** The churn-load kill reproduced the exact original incident shape without any injection: both victim transactions were ATOMIC-SKIP'd as untagged, the replay refused (rc=-117), and containment held perfectly — one refuser, durable AG-mask publish, 31/31 quarantine import, zero shutdowns, all mounts intact. This satisfies the sess328 Q2(a) "genuinely unapplied POLICY path" requirement.

**Genuine shape-4 mid-replay TORN fired — and found defect #91.** After teaching the driver a pure-inode victim workload (only `XFS_LI_INODE` items genuinely apply on foreign replay; anything with BUF/ICREATE items is ATOMIC-SKIP'd and never reaches the countdown), the injection fired with a real 2-item applied prefix and the TORN/FSWIDE verdict published and propagated — but the elected replayer's **own live filesystem shut down**. Root proven to the exact line: `xlog_do_recovery_pass` calls `xlog_force_shutdown(shadow_log)` to stale partial-checkpoint buffers, and the shadow's `l_mp` is the survivor's live mount. Any natural torn foreign slice with ≥1 applied item hits this in production — survivor suicide of exactly the class D-513 forbids.

**Ledgered and ruled.** New entry `D-FOREIGN-SHADOW-UNWIND-HOST-SHUTDOWN-513B` (critical, #91, linked to #90). GPT ruling obtained and stored: fix is a buffer-layer `xfs_buf_delwri_fail()` (no-I/O failure completion, never touching mount shutdown state) wired into the untrusted-replay error arm, plus a provenance audit of every shutdown site and iodone chain reachable from the shadow replay.

Criteria not met — 39 defects open (27 critical). Next session: implement #91 per the ruling, review, re-prep, and re-run shape 4 to zero shutdowns.

